@page "/theming"

<PageTitle>Theming — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Theming</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A theme is a block of custom properties. Switch it in the header and watch every component on
    this page change without a rebuild — nothing a theme sets is resolved by Tailwind.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">The tokens, live</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Every swatch below reads its own variable (<code>style="background:var(--primary)"</code>),
    so flipping the header switcher repaints this whole grid with zero rebuild. That is the
    entire theming model: tokens, not overrides.
</p>

<div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5">
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--primary)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--primary</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--secondary)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--secondary</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--muted)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--muted</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--accent)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--accent</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--destructive)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--destructive</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg border" style="background:var(--card)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--card</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--chart-1)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--chart-1</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--chart-2)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--chart-2</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--chart-3)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--chart-3</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border p-3"><span class="block h-12 rounded-lg" style="background:var(--ring)"></span><p class="mt-2 text-xs font-medium">--ring</p></div>
</div>

<p class="doc-note">
    shadcn's own tokens, plus six this port adds so that another design language has somewhere
    to land: <code>--control-h</code>, <code>--control-text</code>, <code>--radius-control</code>,
    <code>--elevation-1..4</code>, <code>--ease-ui</code>, <code>--duration-ui</code>, plus
    <code>--font-numeric</code>. All additive — they change no class string, so they cost nothing
    in parity.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Six themes, one markup</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Each card sets <code>data-theme</code> on itself, so six themes render side by side from the
    exact same components. This is also how an app ships one theme: put it on
    <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> and ship one file.
</p>

